The Providence is the strider built at [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]], a platform on eight legs with buildings set on top, three or four stories up. Its name was given by the leader of the [[Phenomena/Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]], who built it with some of his Istrian companions to carry pilgrims to the Void Side Wall.

It stands about three quarters of a mile wide on legs some three hundred feet tall, eight to a side and offset so they clear each other as it walks, which gives it something of a spider or centipede in its build. The lower body holds the machinery that drives the legs. Above it is the city: buildings, shops and a banquet hall toward the middle, and open transplanted grassland around the outer edge, where each keystone-holder is granted a plot of land a quarter mile on a side. Above the buildings, unlike a common strider, rises a fourth layer of interlocking rings set with turning, scoop-shaped apparatus, which the builders added for the long crossing.

Below decks the Providence keeps a parking garage, reached by an elevator with buttons for the garage and the surface only; the engine room is closed to guests. The upper floors hold the banquet hall, which must be reserved, a store, a gym, a fortune-telling Harlequin, and a small repository where scrolls can be made to order at a higher price than at home. Below deck are the machinery and the basic workman's tools. A Harlequin servant is assigned to each berth, and guests may request an audience with [[Org/The Harlequins/People/The Master of Ceremonies|the Master]], who keeps to himself.

The first guests aboard, at berth 6, are the [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/index|Hildebrandt Corporation]], who brought two heavy armored cars tied together on a single [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystone]]; the Party holds berth 14. The Providence is to leave six days after the Party boards, with a banquet the evening it departs.
